=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7 SchemaDriftPage and the
  W-0084 ConflictWarnings feature-view do. The generated prompt's idealized "ConflictWarnings.xaml +
  ConflictWarningsViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Automations" is mapped onto these real conventions.
- PREDECESSOR (no bypass): the ConflictWarnings surface already exists from feature-view prompt W-0084
  (.github/prompts/monorepo/logs/p2-windows-feature-views-0084-ConflictWarnings.log, committed 4658032ff) with
  the loading / empty / ready branches. The PAGE manifest record (apps/parity/parity-manifest.json
  id=page:automations/ConflictWarnings) declares states=[empty,error] + string=automations.builder.conflict,
  requiredCount=3. The page-parity delta over W-0084 is therefore the ERROR data state. This run EXTENDS the
  existing presentational surface (DRY; honours the predecessor) rather than duplicating it — one surface, raised
  to the page-parity bar.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest declares NO API data sources — the web component binds only
  useTranslation and renders host-resolved props (the hosting AutomationBuilderPage derives `conflicts` from its
  save/validate mutation). So there is no generated-client Source/ViewModel to add; the bound C# state holder is
  ConflictWarningsModel (the web `conflicts` prop + the parent-driven Loading / HasError lifecycle flags), and all
  branch selection, severity parsing, variant/glyph mapping and copy resolution happen in the WinUI-free
  ConflictWarningsProjection (headless-tested). The view performs no HTTP.
- The 3 data states are visible Fluent regions per ADR-006 (never a blank region), branch precedence
  loading → error → empty → ready (ConflictWarningsProjection.SelectState):
    loading -> ConflictWarnings.cs#BuildLoading: a polite LiveRegion StackPanel of TsSkeleton banner rows.
    error   -> ConflictWarnings.cs#BuildError: a TsQueryError (InfoBar-equivalent, assertive live region, danger
               glyph) carrying ErrorTitle/ErrorMessage + a Retry affordance (ActionText=RetryLabel). The view
               performs no fetch, so Retry raises the public ConflictWarnings.RetryRequested event for the host
               (AutomationBuilderPage) to re-run the conflict check. The error branch overrides empty/ready (a
               failed check has no trustworthy conflict list) but never overrides loading.
    empty   -> ConflictWarnings.cs#BuildEmpty: a TsEmptyState (the native always-render replacement for the web's
               bare `return null`).
    ready   -> ConflictWarnings.cs#BuildReady: the web composition — a `space-y-2` StackPanel of one
               non-dismissible TsAlertBanner per conflict (severity-mapped variant + glyph, the shared
               "Potential Conflict" heading and the `"name": reason` body).
- i18n: the ONLY i18n key in the web source is automations.builder.conflict ("Potential Conflict"). It and the
  shared empty/loading copy were already wired by W-0084 (translation.automations.builder.conflict +
  translation.common.noData/loading). The new error surface reuses the web QueryError generic-failure copy that
  already exists in the catalog — translation.error.network.title ("Can't reach server"),
  translation.error.network.message ("Check your internet connection and try again.") and
  translation.error.retry ("Retry"). NO new strings were added (all present in Strings/en/Resources.resw; the
  he/ar catalogs lag en by design and fall back to the English default via ILocalizer). Every label resolves
  through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names.
- a11y: each state sets a Narrator name on the surface (ConflictWarningsDisplay.AutomationName: loading→loading
  label, error→error title, empty→empty message, ready→"Potential Conflict"); the error surface is an assertive
  live region with the danger glyph; the loading surface is a polite live region; each banner carries a
  "Title. Message" Narrator name. Light/dark honoured via design tokens (TsColor*Brush) on the shared components.
- SI units N/A (no unit-bearing fields on this surface — only automation names / reasons / a severity token).
- Navigation: web route is (unrouted) — ConflictWarnings is a host-embedded presentational component, not a
  routed screen, so there is no NavigationView entry / deep link to register (consistent with W-0084 and the web
  source). Out-of-scope items rejected: no other pages, no backend changes, no new features, no web pixel-cloning.
- Files changed (4): ConflictWarnings.Model.cs (+ Error state, HasError/Failed, error copy consts, error-branch
  projection), ConflictWarnings.cs (+ RetryRequested event, BuildError, Error switch case),
  ConflictWarningsTests.cs (+7 headless tests), apps/parity/windows-ledger.json (page row covered). 0 files
  touched under TeslaSync.App.UITests/.

